---
import { docHref, docs } from '../../data/site-links';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<header class="section-header">
  <span class="eyebrow">Everywhere you run it</span>
  <h2>Same command on your laptop, in a hook, in a container, in CI.</h2>
</header>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Watch mode</h3>
    <p>
      Only the tools matching the changed file run, derived from each tool's own file patterns.
      <a href={docHref(base, docs.watchMode)}>Watch mode guide</a>.
    </p>
    <dl class="map">
      <dt>*.py</dt><dd>ruff · mypy · bandit · black</dd>
      <dt>*.ts</dt><dd>oxlint · tsc</dd>
      <dt>*.rs</dt><dd>clippy · rustfmt</dd>
      <dt>*.yaml</dt><dd>yamllint · prettier</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Output formats</h3>
    <p>One flag, eight renderers, one findings model.</p>
    <div class="fmt-list">
      <code>grid</code><code>plain</code><code>json</code><code>sarif</code><code>github</code><code>markdown</code><code>html</code><code>csv</code>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>GitHub Actions</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>PR comment with results</li>
      <li><code>github</code> format for inline annotations</li>
      <li>SARIF upload to code scanning</li>
      <li><code>--diff</code> for PR-scoped runs</li>
      <li>AI review workflow with trusted install</li>
    </ul>
    <a href={docHref(base, docs.githubIntegration)}>GitHub integration guide</a>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>pre-commit</h3>
    <p>
      Run Lintro as a hook and keep one unified output instead of each hook's raw text.
      <a href={docHref(base, docs.preCommit)}>Hook setup</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Docker</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><code>ghcr.io/lgtm-hq/py-lintro</code> with every tool installed</li>
      <li><code>ghcr.io/lgtm-hq/py-lintro-base</code> CLI only</li>
    </ul>
    <a href={docHref(base, docs.docker)}>Docker guide</a>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>No Python at all</h3>
    <p>
      <code>bun add -g @lgtm-hq/lintro</code> installs a self-contained native binary for
      darwin-arm64, darwin-x64, linux-arm64 or linux-x64. Homebrew via <code>lgtm-hq/tap</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .section-header {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .card {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    background: var(--wb-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--wb-hair);
    border-radius: var(--wb-radius);
  }

  .card h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--wb-muted);
  }

  .card ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3px;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 16px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--wb-muted);
  }

  .card a {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--turbo-link-default, var(--wb-ink));
  }

  .fmt-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .fmt-list code {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .map {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: 6px 14px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .map dt {
    font-family: var(--wb-font-mono);
    color: var(--wb-ink);
  }

  .map dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--wb-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--wb-muted);
  }
</style>
